    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d478">

                <pb facs="0905" n="845" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg845"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Hovey.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 74.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-01-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 15, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I inclose for your information a copy of a
                        dispatch<anchor n="*" xml:id="d478-f1"/> which I have this day addressed to
                    Judson Kilpatrick, esq., minister plenipotentiary, &amp;c., accredited by the
                    United States near the government of the republic of Chili, in relation to the
                    mediation offered on behalf of this government between the Queen of Spain and
                    the allied republics of South America.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvin P. Hovey</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d478-f1" n="*" xml:id="d478-f1-content">
                <p>For this inclosure see instruction No. 55, of the 15th of January, to the United
                    States minister to Chili, p. 315.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
